  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jinja Regional Referral Hospital (JRRH) Strengthening Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  JRRH is a government-to-government award that supports Uganda&apos;s Ministry of Health (MOH) to bridge the gap between the central and district levels of the health system. JRRH will enhance the oversight and coordination functions of the MOH at lower levels to maximize effectiveness and efficiency gains. FY 2022 nutrition and maternal and child health (MCH) funds will leverage PEPFAR support to this activity and build a regional platform for quality improvement in family planning service delivery and maternal, newborn, and child health services, including Maternal and Perinatal Death Surveillance and Response. TB funds will strengthen drug resistance case management in the JRRH and improve TB treatment success rate to 90%. Nutrition, TB and MCH funds will contribute to cross-cutting Health Systems Support.JRRH will serve as a center of excellence for reproductive, family planning, maternal, neonatal, adolescent, and child health and nutrition services in 11 districts, while ensuring the reduction of gender-based violence and promotion of gender equality. JRRH will act as a regional capacity building hub and as a central platform for sustainable skills transfer to the lower-level health facilities.JRRH will prioritize: 1) implementing improved regional hospital-district patient referral and information flow; 2) data-driven decision making and knowledge management; 3) standardization of supportive supervision and policy dissemination; 4) quality assurance; and 5) district and regional level planning and coordination. JRRH will fund activities to: 1) improve gender equality and empower women to access and use high quality health services; 2) prevent gender-based violence and address the impact of gender-based violence; 3) improve nutrition outcomes; and 4) build the capacity of health facilities to strengthen outreach and mobile clinics to ensure continuity of services during climate-related disruptions..</narrative>
  </description>
